  "worked_solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(-2,1),(1,1),$ and $(1,-2).$\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(-2,1)}=(1)^{2}-(1)=0, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,1)}=(1)^{2}-(1)=0, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(1,-2)}=(-2)^{2}-(-2)=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040222/assets/5f2f99159626fad30330210592c4e36859bfc30d7d3cf2c3f9178e1cb93498aa.png)",
